## Email strategy (SDE3: conservative, not spammy)

Email is higher-friction than push. Emailing for every in-app event will cause
unsubscribes and spam-folder routing. Only send email for genuinely actionable,
high-value events:

| Notification type | In-app | Email | Rationale |
|-------------------|--------|-------|-----------|
| `event_new` | ✅ | ✅ | Student needs to register before deadline |
| `deadline` 48h | ✅ | ✅ | Enough lead time to act |
| `deadline` 4h | ✅ | ❌ | Too late for email to be useful; in-app only |
| `credential_update` | ✅ | ✅ | Student needs to know if cert was rejected |
| `link_received` | ✅ | ❌ | Team-finder is casual; email would feel spammy |
| `link_update` | ✅ | ❌ | In-app is sufficient for accept/decline |
| `link_expiring` | ✅ | ❌ | In-app only; expiry is low-urgency |

**Rule:** Email is a transactional notification, not a real-time alert.

