## Key design decisions

| Decision | Rationale |
|----------|-----------|
| Email-only, no web push | Simpler, no VAPID key management, no PushSubscription model, works on all browsers including iOS immediately |
| Conservative email (3 types, not 7) | Email is high-friction; spamming causes unsubscribes + spam-folder routing. Push is real-time; email is not |
| `deadline` 4h → in-app only | 4h before deadline, email is too slow to be actionable |
| `sendNotification()` is `void` not `async` | Spec: "notification sending never blocks API response" |
| Emails use `user.email` from User model | Students' emails are already stored from F-1 registration — no separate storage needed |
| `AuditLog` for deadline dedup, not Event field | Reuses indexed model; keeps Event schema free of scheduling concerns (SRP) |
| Cursor pagination on Notification | Offset pagination loses rows on fast-inserting collections; ObjectId cursor is stable and monotonic |
| `invalidateCachePrefix('home:')` on new event | All students could be affected; prefix-wipe is O(k) in-process where k = active user count |
| `invalidateCache('home:${userId}')` on link events | Targeted — only the affected user's home invalidated |
| Delete `StudentHomePage` | It is fully superseded; keeping it invites confusion and dead code |
| `useHome().data?.unreadNotificationsFlag` drives BottomNav dot | `useHome` is already called on mount and staleTime=30s; free signal, no extra query |

